menu "Bot audio interactions"
    config BOT_AUDIO_ENABLE
        bool "Enable optional microphone audio service"
        default n
        help
            Enable microphone audio processing for environmental sound response.
            When enabled, the bot can respond to environmental sounds with
            facial expressions. When disabled, no audio hardware is initialized.
            Default is n (disabled) per privacy-first design.

    config BOT_AUDIO_G0_VERIFIED
        bool "Board audio contract physically verified (release gate)"
        default n
        depends on BOT_AUDIO_ENABLE
        help
            Enable runtime microphone requests only after the board-specific
            G0 input, stop and resource report has passed. Compile success is
            not verification. Probe builds bypass this gate, never normal UI.

    config BOT_AUDIO_DIAGNOSTICS
        bool "Enable audio diagnostics logging"
        default n
        depends on BOT_AUDIO_ENABLE
        help
            Enable low-frequency diagnostic logging of audio processing.
            Logs include RMS levels, event counts, and service state.
            No PCM data is logged. Maximum 1 Hz log rate.

    config BOT_AUDIO_G0_PROBE
        bool "G0 audio contract probe (development verification only)"
        default n
        help
            Runs a bounded hardware contract probe at boot INSTEAD of the
            normal UI: verifies init/open/read timing/short reads/close and
            prints a "@g0 {...}" summary. Does not start LVGL or the IMU.
            Operator must keep quiet for phase A, then clap/talk for phase B.
            DEVELOPMENT ONLY - do not ship. Requires BOT_AUDIO_ENABLE.
        depends on BOT_AUDIO_ENABLE
endmenu